        contracts: ["medical-procedures", "emergency-procedures"],
        backstory: "Yael was created in a Geneweaver Vault — a classified research program that spliced human DNA with xenological samples recovered from a Predecessor ruin. They were designed as a biological blank slate: adaptable, intelligent, and emotionally stable to the point of detachment. When the vault's security was breached during a corporate raid, Yael escaped into the chaos. They have spent the years since hiding, using their medical abilities to secure passage on ships that don't ask questions. The Loup-Garou is their longest stay anywhere. They know the Geneweavers are still searching. They do not know what the Geneweavers will do when they find them.",
        secrets: [
            (
                id: "yael_geneweaver",
                reveal_condition: all([
                    compare(field: "trust.player", op: gt, value: 768),
                    compare(field: "event.asked_about_geneweaver", op: eq, value: 1),
                ]),
                content: "Yael is not a xenotype in the natural sense — they were designed as a proof of concept for a human-xeno hybrid soldier program. The Geneweavers implanted a subdermal tracker that went dormant when Yael fled, but they have no way to know if it's truly offline or merely waiting for an activation signal. Every time the ship passes a deep-space relay, Yael expects the tracker to wake up and lead their creators straight to them.",
